  "body": "Stacked on #204 (issue/152-short-bar-axis). Retarget to main before #204 merges; the two merge back to back, never #204 alone.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe axis fit no longer trusts an axis whose inlier normal lines all meet at ONE point (P0: a trusted wrong axis = every turned or cross-drilled feature about the wrong line).\n\n- New `multiaxis/axis_point.rs`, called from `judge` in `axis.rs`. It finds the least-squares point where the inlier normal lines meet, then refits on the half of the area that misses it least. If lines through that point carry ≥ half the inlier area, those facets alone must pass the coarseness gate about the axis. Lines through one point carry no direction, so they can stand for a turned part only if they themselves cover every bearing.\n- A box's faces give 2–4 bearings about any axis, and a single-band wall gives 2 about a cross axis: both are refused. A single-band wall about its OWN axis gives every bearing, so the common one-band CAD cylinder still fits. Multi-band walls are untouched.\n- On isotropic parts, an axis read off a facing flat is no longer tilted by the direction refinement.\n- The bearing-gap gate moved into the new module; `axis.rs` is 385 lines.\n- Known cost: a single-band shaft whose keyway or D-flat leaves a bearing gap over about 28° is refused rather than read. It fails closed.\n- Options dropped (RECOMMENDED.md):\n  - sub-sampling faces, which breaks the exact meeting point coarse turned meshes rely on;\n  - axial spread or a refusal for any point-concurrency, which would refuse the single-band cylinder;\n  - a second-moment symmetry test, since a square plate is symmetric about its own normal.\n\n## Pins (`axis_point_tests.rs`), each failing on the base 7fff05c\n\n- `a_plate_with_a_boss_off_its_centre_line_is_refused_by_name` (100×100×10, r5 boss at (10,0), 1 and 5 bands): was trusted at (0.707, 0, 0.707)\n- `a_single_band_shaft_with_a_flat_and_a_cross_hole_is_not_read_across` (r10 h150): was trusted X\n- `a_cube_with_an_off_centre_boss_is_refused_by_name` (60 mm cube, r5 boss at (10,10), 1 and 5 bands): was trusted, tilted 15°\n- Guard: `a_single_band_bar_still_fits_its_true_axis` (h20 and h150, off-origin)\n\nAll earlier pins stay correct: turned bar, short bars, keyed shafts, the #116 punched bar, noisy shafts, plate with a centred hole, cube, sphere, prism and #204's plate with a boss.\n\n## Readings\n\nmotion lib axis 47; multiaxis*, rotary* and turning_* green; app drilling_cross* (all), lathe_* and turning* green (21 suites); clippy on motion and app is clean.\n\nChangelog: The lathe and rotary axis fit refuses by name a part whose normals only meet at one point (a plate or block with a turned boss, a single-band shaft read across) instead of trusting a wrong axis\n\nFixes #208\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
